From: nemo-speech-python
Subject: asr: bound the RNNT greedy decoder's speculative joint window

RnntGreedyDecoder evaluates the joint for every remaining encoder frame in
one graph and keeps the leading run of blanks. Each emitted token changes the
predictor state and starts a new round over all remaining frames, so offline
decoding costs tokens x frames, quadratic in the audio length. On the CPU this
makes long offline recognition with RNNT models (nemotron-3.5) much slower
than the encoder: 63 s for 80 s of audio, against 17.5 s for transcribe.cpp
(nemo-speech-python #56).

Evaluate at most 16 frames per round, and move on to the next window under
the same predictor state when a window is all blank. A frame's joint depends
only on that frame and the predictor state, so the decoded tokens are
unchanged; a round now costs a bounded amount of work.
---
diff --git a/src/asr/decoders/rnnt_greedy_decoder.cpp b/src/asr/decoders/rnnt_greedy_decoder.cpp
index 8b36670..3a0f59a 100644
--- a/src/asr/decoders/rnnt_greedy_decoder.cpp
+++ b/src/asr/decoders/rnnt_greedy_decoder.cpp
@@ -242,8 +242,14 @@ RnntGreedyDecoder::step_impl(
     token_ids_.resize(static_cast<size_t>(T));
     int t = 0;
     int symbols_at_frame = 0;
+    // nemo-speech-python: evaluate at most kJointWindow frames per round. A
+    // round otherwise covers every remaining frame, and a new round starts
+    // at each emitted token, so decoding cost grew with tokens x frames
+    // (quadratic in the audio length). Each frame's joint depends only on
+    // that frame and the predictor state, so the decisions are unchanged.
+    constexpr int kJointWindow = 16;
     while (t < T) {
-        const int remaining = T - t;
+        const int remaining = std::min(T - t, kJointWindow);
         const float* boost_bias = nullptr;
         if (bias_on_) {
             // NeMo/riva semantics (rnnt_label_looping.py): blank vs non-blank is
@@ -321,8 +327,11 @@ RnntGreedyDecoder::step_impl(
             }
         }
         if (first_emit < 0) {
-            // Every remaining frame is blank under this predictor state.
-            break;
+            // Every frame of this window is blank under this predictor state:
+            // go on with the next window under the same state.
+            t += remaining;
+            symbols_at_frame = 0;
+            continue;
         }
 
